  "contribution": {
    "summary": "Qualify a new dw.quantities.expression calendar NuGet candidate with exactly one dependency on the previously published dw.quantities archive and a compiled source-free binary consumer.",
    "value": "Preserve original source ProjectReference and Version, link three original C# files in a temporary packaging project, use the existing NuGet F1 calendar preview and package reader, pin the published dependency and run six independent dual-DLL checks.",
    "debtChanges": [
      "Math source project versions and original ProjectReference remain unchanged; only the disposable package projection uses an exact NuGet dependency.",
      "RS138 produces an unreserved, unpublished Expression candidate; its publisher rehearsal, immutable NUGET_LOCAL release and readback remain later explicit gates.",
      "Package-specific notices and third-party rights remain unapproved for public distribution; installed package rollback and other OS platforms are not qualified.",
      "dw.quantities.standard requires both independently published base and Expression packages; never infer that candidate qualification establishes a published dependency."
    ],
    "nextAction": "After RS138 succeeds, inspect the exact Expression candidate/dependency hashes and qualify an isolated no-overwrite publisher rehearsal; only separately authorize private local publication and then qualify the published binary before advancing standard units.",
